    "https://careers.wlu.ca/job/Other-PD300-VA1-Research-Methods-I-W27/1291653247/": {
      "title": "PD300 VA1",
      "description": "PD300 VA1 - Research Methods I - W27 Job Details | Wilfrid Laurier University Skip to main content Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Sign Into My Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: PD300 VA1 - Research Methods I - W27 Apply now » Date: Oct 13, 2026 Location: Other, CA Company: Wilfrid Laurier University Faculty/Academic Area: Faculty of Human & Social Sciences Department : N/A Campus: Other Employee Group: WLUFA Requisition ID: 11904 Position Title: PD300 VA1 – Research Methods I – W27 Term: Winter 2027 (January 4 – April 30, 2027) Days/Hours Total: 3 per week/36 total Mode of Delivery: Virtual Asynchronous Type of Instruction: Anticipated Class Size: 75 Additional Course Requirements: None Posted on: October 13, 2026 Posting ends: October 18, 2026 Position Summary: An introduction to statistical and geographic research methods, with an emphasis on the understanding and use of these procedures in law enforcement. Students will become familiar with designing research questions, constructing hypotheses, identifying types of variables, assessing reliability and validity, selecting appropriate research methods and understanding elementary quantitative and spatial data analysis. Qualifications – Required: Master’s Degree Qualifications – Discipline: Public Administration, Public Safety, Business, Leadership Qualifications - Other: Doctorate preferred. Significant work experience and/or research in a field related to course content, specifically in law enforcement, in particular areas of leadership 