    "https://careers.wlu.ca/job/Waterloo-EN409QA-Contemporary-British-Literature-%28Winter-2027%29-ON/1291643047/": {
      "title": "EN409QA Contemporary British Literature (Winter 2027) Job Details",
      "description": "EN409QA Contemporary British Literature (Winter 2027) Job Details | Wilfrid Laurier University Skip to main content Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Sign Into My Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: EN409QA Contemporary British Literature (Winter 2027) Apply now » Date: Oct 9, 2026 Location: Waterloo, CA Company: Wilfrid Laurier University Faculty/Academic Area: Faculty of Arts Department : English and Film Studies Campus: Waterloo Employee Group: WLUFA Requisition ID: 11901 Position Title: EN409Q Contemporary British Literature Term: Winter 2027 (January 1-April 30) Days/Times: Tuesday, Thursday 4 – 6:50 p.m. Hours per week/Hours Total: 3/36 Mode of Delivery: In-Person Type of Instruction: Lecture Anticipated Class Size: 22 Additional Course Requirements: None Posted on: October 9, 2026 Posting ends: October 19, 2026 AI tools will be used in the hiring process: No Position Summary: Course description: an exploration of British literature from circa 1970 to the present, covering poetry, drama, and/or prose as they engage with the social demands and complex realities of an ever-changing Britain. Qualifications – Required Academic Degree: PhD Qualifications – Required Discipline: English Qualifications – Required Areas of Specialization: Qualifications – Required Professional Designation: Qualifications – Other Teaching experience at the university-level; Research expertise (dissertation, publications and/or conference presentations) in English is an asset. Salary: $10,212.40 subject to CA 25 (Co